cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If this software is used, please cite it as below."
title: "pentadiagonal-solver: a batched pentadiagonal solver with CUDA optimisations"
authors:
  - family-names: "Agrawal"
    given-names: "Sidhant Kumar"
    affiliation: "University of Warwick"
  - family-names: "Shukla"
    given-names: "Nidhi"
    affiliation: "University of Warwick"
abstract: >-
  A batched pentadiagonal linear-system solver for CPUs and NVIDIA GPUs,
  targeting ADI (Alternating Direction Implicit) workloads. Provides a family
  of memory-bandwidth-optimised CUDA kernels (register-resident POP-PCR/SPIKE,
  fused on-chip-transpose Thomas, and an ADI-structured shared-coefficient
  solver) that reach 8–11x speedups over a multi-core CPU baseline.
keywords:
  - pentadiagonal solver
  - CUDA
  - GPU
  - ADI
  - Thomas algorithm
  - SPIKE
  - PCR
  - high performance computing
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/SidhantKrAgrawal/pentadiagonal-solver"
